.TH "YAMLR-LICENSES" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-licenses \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBThird-Party License Attribution\fR
.PP
The \fBlicenses\fR command displays the official list of third-party open-source libraries used within the Yamlr binary and their respective licenses.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr licenses
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
To maintain full intellectual property transparency and open-source license compliance, Yamlr includes a comprehensive manifest of all dependencies and their licensing terms (MIT, Apache 2.0, BSD, etc.).
.PP
.SH "OUTPUT"
The command prints a list of:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  Library Name
.IP "\(bu" 2
  Version
.IP "\(bu" 2
  License Type
.IP "\(bu" 2
  Full License Text (via pager)
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
yamlr licenses
.RE
.fi
.SH "COMPLIANCE NOTE"
Yamlr is built with a "Zero-GPL" policy in the core engine to ensure maximum commercial flexibility and compatibility with proprietary enterprise environments.
.PP
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/yamlr/yamlr/issues>
.PP
